From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: compiled XAML (XBF v2) -- pages as applications ship them

Applications ship their pages compiled (.xbf), as files or inside their resource index; there was no reader. The file layout -- header, string, assembly, namespace, type, property and XML namespace tables, node sections, node opcodes and value encodings -- and the framework's type and property numbering (xbf_ids.txt, data, generated into xbf_ids.h by make_xbf_ids.py) are per XbfAnalyzer (Apache-2.0), the open-source XBF analyser; the reader is ours and copies no code. Its nodes drive the same object writer as XAML text: framework and application types, properties set from values (booleans, numbers, strings, thicknesses, grid lengths, colours, enums), collections, x:Name, x:ConnectionId; styles, resources, visual states and data templates are read past (not applied yet); deferred elements are made. Application.LoadComponent finds a page's .xbf next to its .xaml path or in the package's resource index (Files/..., embedded data; windows.applicationmodel's PRI reader, now with pri_get_data, built in as well). The input comes from arbitrary applications: every read, table index, offset and count is checked, nesting and section recursion are bounded, and a bad file fails the load. Behind the XAML switch of 6131.
---
diff --git a/dlls/windows.applicationmodel/pri.c b/dlls/windows.applicationmodel/pri.c
index e235ddf..07fba7d 100644
--- a/dlls/windows.applicationmodel/pri.c
+++ b/dlls/windows.applicationmodel/pri.c
@@ -953,6 +953,29 @@ WCHAR *pri_get_string( const struct pri_file *pri, const WCHAR *path, const WCHA
     return NULL;
 }
 
+const unsigned char *pri_get_data( const struct pri_file *pri, const WCHAR *path, size_t *len )
+{
+    WCHAR buf[1024];
+    unsigned int i, j;
+
+    for (i = 0; i < pri->schema.num_items; i++)
+    {
+        const struct item_candidates *ic = &pri->map[i];
+
+        if (!ic->count) continue;
+        item_path( pri, i, buf, sizeof(buf) / sizeof(buf[0]) );
+        if (!path_equal( buf, path )) continue;
+        for (j = 0; j < ic->count; j++)
+        {
+            if (ic->c[j].value_type != VT_EMBEDDED) continue;
+            *len = ic->c[j].len;
+            return ic->c[j].data;
+        }
+        return NULL;
+    }
+    return NULL;
+}
+
 void pri_enum_items( const struct pri_file *pri, void (*cb)( const WCHAR *path, void *ctx ), void *ctx )
 {
     WCHAR buf[1024];
